Task: German Legal Named Entity Recognition
Description: Recognize named entities in German legal text. Entities to look for: organisation. German capitalizes all nouns, so rules must use strong context anchors 

Input schema: {'text': 'str'}
Output schema:
entities: List[Entity]

Entity:
  text: string  # The matched text span
  start: integer  # Start character offset
  end: integer  # End character offset
  type: string  # Entity label

AVAILABLE ENTITY TYPES: ['organisation']
Rules MUST use one of these types in output_template.


DATA EVIDENCE FROM TRAINING:
- organisation (15 unique): "Energie Verdorfwald GmbH", "Landesgericht Leoben", "Bundesministeriums f\u00fcr Finanzen", "Landesgerichtes", "Gerichtshof der Europ\u00e4ischen Union", "St. Johann Steuerberatung GmbH", "APP Steuerberatung GmbH", "Schlaich Bau KG", "Magistrates der Stadt Wien, Magistratsabteilung 67", "Magistrat der Stadt Wien, Magistratsabteilung 67", "Landespolizeidirektion Wien", "Magistrat der Stadt Wien", "Frieb - Causa Steuerberatung GmbH", "Fritzenwallner-Gandler Wirtschaftstreuhand- und Steuerberatungsgesellschaft mbH", "Dreissigacker M\u00f6bel"
  Exact pattern: (?:Fri(?:tzenwallner\-Gandler Wirtschaftstreuhand\- und Steuerberatungsgesellschaft |eb \- Causa Steuerberatung G)mbH|Magistrat(?:es)? der Stadt Wien, Magistratsabteilung 67|Gerichtshof der Europäischen Union|(?:Bundesministeriums für Finanz|Landes(?:polizeidirektion Wi|gericht Leob))en|(?:(?:St\. Johann|APP) Steuerberatung|Energie Verdorfwald) GmbH|Magistrat der Stadt Wien|Dreissigacker Möbel|Landesgerichtes|Schlaich Bau KG)
  In context: "... Ende 2014 an die [Energie Verdorfwald GmbH] (deren...", "Das [Landesgericht Leoben] hat den BF mit...", "...die  Auskunft des [Bundesministeriums f\u00fcr Finanzen] vom 21.05.2021,...", "...Feststellung des [Landesgerichtes] X, wonach der BF ...", "...brachte beim [Gerichtshof der Europ\u00e4ischen Union] (EuGH) eine ..."

Note: Some entities contain multiple words; do NOT assume single-token matches.

Computed patterns match training strings only; generalize carefully.


COORDINATOR GUIDANCE (prioritize this):
Prioritize the 'organisation' class immediately as it suffers from a severe recall deficit (R=12%) and high false positive rate, indicating the current rules are too restrictive or noisy. The rule generator should attempt to broaden positive patterns for this class while introducing specific negative constraints to filter out the 183 false positives, rather than adding more general rules. Avoid further generalization without targeted negative examples, as this will likely exacerbate the existing precision issues.


PER-CLASS METRICS (current performance):
  organisation: P=16% R=12% F1=14% (TP=35 FP=183 FN=255)

RULES with failures (full details, note any user_feedback on specific rules):
[
  {
    "name": "GmbH_entities",
    "description": "Matches companies ending in GmbH, including variations with 'Fa.' prefix or hyphens.",
    "format": "regex",
    "content": "(?:Fa\\.)?([A-Z][a-zA-Z0-9\\s\\-]+(?:\\s+und\\s+[A-Z][a-zA-Z0-9\\s]+)?\\s+GmbH)",
    "priority": 9,
    "output_template": {
      "text": "$1",
      "start": "$start",
